# A scout cannot step to a territory its own does not touch.
#
# **`{refused}` says what the rule needed and did not find.** Territory 1 touches 2 and 2 touches
# 3; nothing says 1 touches 3, so `move`'s second clause asks for an adjacency that is not there.

{test name:the-scout-cannot-cross-where-there-is-no-border}

{given}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{territory id:2 name:territory-2}
{territory id:3 name:territory-3}
{adjacency id:1 from:territory-1 to:territory-2}
{adjacency id:2 from:territory-2 to:territory-3}
{residency what:scout where:territory-1} -> 1

{when}
{move what:scout from:territory-1 to:territory-3}

{refused}
{adjacency from:territory-1 to:territory-3}
